  "behavior": "Opening admits metadata without reading samples. One-based T/C/Z, processor-raw/default and explicit bin/range fields are drafts; invalid drafts disable calculation while preserving the last successful result. Live display navigation does not retarget the draft. Source data/metadata/selection edits or foreign/closed owners disable calculation. The panel retains detached results for export after source closure and releases all captures on close.",
  "presentation": "Log1p count heights leave raw histogram arrays unchanged. Plot hover shows raw intervals/counts. Statistics include visited/finite/NaN/in-range/underflow/overflow, unbinned finite-ROI mean/population SD/min/max/sum, and the first largest-count bin interval. This binned mode is not an exact continuous raw-value mode.",
  "publication": "Export last result CSV freezes native raw CSV text before opening the shared browser. The existing atomic writer/overwrite prompt publishes it. Invalid drafts, log toggles or source edits do not recompute that frozen text. The API also exports detached last results; no analysis pixel/history/workflow record is created.",
  "compatibility": "Legacy Histogram menu/action behavior remains available for legacy types outside the native scalar UInt8/UInt16/Float32 service. New scientific calculation supports the service finite/quiet-NaN policies; broader domains remain open.",
